#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "CAP-REPOSITORIES Repositories by trust"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Each layer is its own repository and the unit of trust for its CI identities."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Layer L0 · domain: delivery"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Separate the code that defines who may change the platform from the code that changes it, so each repository can be trusted for exactly what it holds."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "With workload identity federation a credential trusts a repository, so the repository is the unit of trust ([P2]{1}). A monorepo would let anyone who can edit a pipeline reach every identity. Pinned recipes keep the result the same on any machine and any CI host ([P19]{2})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Bootstrap repository: state store and CI identities, applied by dispatch."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Platform repository: shared stacks and the tenant registry, applied on merge."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Modules repository: tagged releases consumed by the others."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Product repositories: code, jobs and their deployment unit, one per product."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Two remotes are normal: a repository can be mirrored on a second host and carry that host's CI definition beside the first. Only the wrapper differs; every step is a recipe."
msgstr ""

