#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "CAP-REPOSITORIES.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Bootstrap, platform, modules and each product are separate repositories."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "List the repositories; each layer and each product has exactly one."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "CAP-REPOSITORIES.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Each federated credential trusts exactly one repository, so a change in one repository cannot obtain another's identity."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Export every federated credential subject; each names one repository and one protected environment."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "CAP-REPOSITORIES.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Every task runs as a recipe in a pinned toolchain, invoked the same way on a workstation and in CI; CI definitions only call recipes."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Inspect the CI definitions: every step is a toolchain bootstrap or a recipe invocation."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "CAP-REPOSITORIES.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "Published history is never rewritten; a correction is a new change on top."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-repositories.md
msgid "The protected branch refuses force-pushes."
msgstr ""

